# print and a write to io.stdout reach the OS in the order the program runs
# them, a file or a pipe on the other end as well as a terminal: print writes
# its bytes and line break straight to the OS, and no C stdio buffer holds
# them back behind a later write.
main: function is {
    print "one"
    b: Bytes
    b.append from: 116.u8
    b.append from: 119.u8
    b.append from: 111.u8
    b.append from: 10.u8
    bv: b.byteView
    w: io.stdout
    wr: w.write from: bv
    print "three"
}
